inue to do so for sure  and what happens to people in blue  states who rely on the state and local  tax deductions it's an interesting  element of this Alex if you live right  there in New York across the river new  jersey up in connecticut out in  california illinois Maryland  those are higher tax states and they've  been accustomed to being able to deduct  your state and local taxes at this point  it'll be capped at ten thousand dollars  that is a notable deduction still but in  some cases you're gonna have people now  ending up paying higher taxes because  they live in those states and their  local and state property taxes can't be  deducted as much as they were before  that was part of the reason why we are  likely to see at least a handful of  House Republicans from those states  mostly suburban swing districts probably  vote against this plan next week because  they still believe it's unfair to their  constituents all right ed O'Keefe in  Washington this morning ed thanks very  much for being with us  take care
 

